28-14 victory over the Air Force Academy on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              Hughes completed 10 of 17 passes for 113 yards and rushed 12 times for 146 more, giving him a hand in 259 of the Cowboys' 301 yards of offense.\n\n\r\n              Hughes ran 68 yards for a touchdown on the second play from scrimmage for a 7-0 lead and Wyoming (5-3, 4-1 Mountain West Conference) never looked back.\n\n\r\n              Hughes started a drive with a 33-yard run then finished it with 4-yard scoring toss to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5150863/jake-wilson\" target=\"_new\">Jake Wilson</a> for a 14-3 advantage in the second quarter.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://x.com/CFBPlayoff/status/2113819753748041857?s=20\">Hughes, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296622/eric-richardson\" target=\"_new\">Eric Richardson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5258056/samuel-harris\" target=\"_new\">Samuel Harris</a></a> teamed up on a hook-and-ladder play to score with 38 seconds left for a 21-6 advantage at halftime.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5306440/evan-medders\" target=\"_new\">Evan Medders</a> connected with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5223116/grant-wayne\" target=\"_new\">Grant Wayne</a> for a 5-yard score at the end of a 15-play drive, and the Falcons closed within 21-14 after Medders ran it in for two points before leaving with an injury. Medders led the team with 115 yards on 21 carries.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5227257/markell-holman\" target=\"_new\">Markell Holman</a>'s 1-yard plunge capped the scoring with 3:04 left to play for the Cowboys, who have won three in a row.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5309674/carter-cremascoli\" target=\"_new\">Carter Cremascoli</a> kicked two field goals for Air Force (5-2, 3-2), which had a four-game win streak snapped.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Air Force: Hosts Connecticut on Oct. 31.\n\n\r\n              Wyoming: At UNLV on Nov. 7.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-10-24T05:01:45Z"}}